eneralize beyond the studied population"}]}},{"text":"On average self-described high-fiber eaters had a higher daily satiety score (mean 48 vs 45), so the data support a typical difference; but because both SDs are about 12, the distributions overlap substantially, so the data do not support a claim that self-described high-fiber eaters are always higher.","correct":true,"misconception":null},{"text":"Since the mean for self-described high-fiber eaters (48) is greater than for self-described low-fiber eaters (45), every member of self-described high-fiber eaters must have a higher daily satiety score than every member of self-described low-fiber eaters.","correct":false,"misconception":"ignores_variability_claims_every_value","misconception_source":{"tag":"ignores_variability_claims_every_value","label":"Treated a difference in means as a claim about every individual value","evidence":"documented_cr","ek_codes":[],"sources":[{"kind":"fact_pack","ref":"AP_STATISTICS_2027_CED_FACT_PACK.md S10 Unit 1 (1.9) / 'General exam-wide conventions'","note":"on-average differences must not be over-read as claims about all individual values; overlap matters"}]}},{"text":"The claim is correct because self-described high-fiber eaters clearly did better on daily satiety score.","correct":false,"misconception":"restates_claim_without_evidence","misconception_source":{"tag":"restates_claim_without_evidence","label":"Restated the claim without citing statistical evidence","evidence":"documented_cr","ek_codes":[],"sources":[{"kind":"fact_pack","ref":"AP_STATISTICS_2027_CED_FACT_PACK.md S4/S6 (skill 4.B; task verbs) + S10 'General exam-wide conventions'","note":"a justification must reference the statistical evidence, not merely restate the claim"}]}}]},"parts":[{"part_key":"part-a","prompt":"In a survey of eating habits, self-described high-fiber eaters had a mean daily satiety score of 48 points (SD about 12) and self-described low-fiber eaters had a mean of 45 points (SD about 12). A 