ocus rating than students who study mostly in the morning.\" Which statement best justifies whether the data support this claim?","response_modalities":["mcq"],"points":1,"criteria":[{"criterion_key":"part-a-criterion-1","points":1,"description":"Selects the justification that affirms the on-average difference while rejecting the over-strong 'always' claim due to overlap.","required_evidence":"Correct justification type: affirms_average_rejects_overstrong_via_overlap","deterministic_checks":[{"kind":"mcq_key","correct_type":"affirms_average_rejects_overstrong_via_overlap"}],"accepted_variants":[]}]}],"provenance":{"generator":"course_mode_stats_generator/slot_frames.py","frame_id":"FB-4B-COMPARE-01","params":{"scenario":"a survey of study habits","mA":49,"mB":45,"sd":10},"seed":97013,"release_status":"unreleased_generated_pending_review","note":"Authored conceptual frame; correctness from authored justification taxonomy."}}},{"schema_version":"course-mode-generated-0.1","package_id":"slotframe-4b-097014","content_key":"apstat-4b-compare-097014","item_type":"mcq","difficulty":"Medium","exam_pack_ref":{"exam_code":"ap_statistics","cycle":"2026-27"},"taxonomy_refs":[{"scheme_key":"ap-statistics-2026-27","node_key":"unit-1"},{"scheme_key":"ap-statistics-2026-27","node_key":"topic-1.9"},{"scheme_key":"ap-statistics-skills","node_key":"skill-4.B","practice":4}],"cells":[{"topic":"1.9","skill":"4.B"}],"scenario_provenance":{"archetype":"Q2","archetype_label":"Multi-focus on Practices 3 & 4 (analyze data; interpret results)","task_verb":"Justify","practice":4,"modality":"exam_aligned_digital","validity_rules":["OBSERVATIONAL comparison only (no random assignment -> no causal claim)","means differ but spreads overlap so an over-strong claim is refutable"],"sources":[{"kind":"fact_pack","ref":"AP_STATISTICS_2027_CED_FACT_PACK.md S5 (Free-response archetypes)","note":"Section II question archetypes Q1-Q4"},{"kind":"fact_pack","ref":"AP_STATISTICS_2027_CED_FACT_PACK.md S6 (Task